# clinical v1.20 — WARNING. The section narrative written to both undeclared
# spellings a C-CDA import path used before this release, and to neither
# canonical one.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT RECORD. This is not an invented mistake; it is what the
# reference C-CDA import path emitted before v1.20 restated
# clinical:narrativeText as covering C-CDA section text, byte for byte in
# structure: the section's text lands on cascade:narrativeText, a predicate
# core never defines, and a second time on clinical:content, a predicate
# clinical never defines either. Both JSON-LD contexts already mapped the
# short name narrativeText to clinical:narrativeText, so a record shaped like
# this one had its only note text sitting on two predicates nothing
# constrained and no context read back. Writing the same text to both
# predicates rather than choosing one is the importer's actual behavior this
# fixture is evidence about, not two independent defects.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT. It asserts
# that clinical:NarrativeTextSpellingShape notices BOTH predicates: two
# sh:Warning results, one per spelling (the shape's two sh:targetSubjectsOf
# declarations union, so the record is reached once and reports once per
# predicate that fires). It asserts equally that NOTHING REJECTS the record --
# the narrative is optional at the shape level, so, as with the v1.19
# medication effective dates, there is no sh:or window to fail and no pod
# fails today for carrying either legacy spelling. The warning is the entire
# migration window.
#
# The record carries NO clinical:narrativeText, which is what a converter that
# has not yet been changed produces. clinical:documentType is left out
# entirely so this fixture isolates the narrative-spelling axis; a document
# exercising clinical:DocumentTypeShape's own warning is a separate fixture.
#
# THIS FIXTURE IS WHAT CLOSES THE WINDOW. clinical v1.20 says
# NarrativeTextSpellingShape is removed once the warning is observably absent
# from conforming output. Until the C-CDA converter writes
# clinical:narrativeText, this fixture warns; when the window closes it must
# be retired in the same commit that removes the shape, and its continuing to
# warn is the record that the window is still open.
#
# Fully synthetic. Same clinic, visit shape and section content as
# document-ccda-section-narrative.VALID.ttl, differing only in which
# predicate carries the text and in carrying it twice, so the two records are
# comparable term for term.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:d0c00116-0000-4000-8000-000000000005> a clinical:ClinicalDocument ;
    clinical:displayName "Progress Note" ;
    clinical:documentDate "2031-04-02"^^xsd:date ;
    clinical:status "final" ;
    clinical:documentReferenceStatus "current" ;

    # Same section narrative as the VALID sibling, written to BOTH undeclared
    # spellings and to neither canonical one.
    cascade:narrativeText "Continue lisinopril 20 mg once daily. Increase walking to 30 minutes five days a week as tolerated. Recheck basic metabolic panel and blood pressure in six weeks. Patient verbalized understanding of the plan and voiced no questions at the close of the visit." ;
    clinical:content "Continue lisinopril 20 mg once daily. Increase walking to 30 minutes five days a week as tolerated. Recheck basic metabolic panel and blood pressure in six weeks. Patient verbalized understanding of the plan and voiced no questions at the close of the visit." ;

    clinical:documentAuthorName "Dara Fennimore, MD" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceId "DocumentReference/dr-56411" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceType "DocumentReference" ;
    clinical:importedAt "2031-04-05T09:40:12-05:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:sourceIdentity "org:meridian" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
